{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1310325-lycian-characters-c20-player-guide","id":1310325,"title":"Lycian Characters (C20 Player Guide)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-05-06T11:21:24-07:00","id":1310325,"title":"Lycian Characters (C20 Player Guide)","content":"First off, I love the concept of Chimera player characters. I generally allow such creatures for players that cannot make regular gaming sessions, and as &quot;stock&quot; characters for new players. And the Lycians allow such characters suitable for main characters.<br /> <br /> For my own use as a Storyteller, I would have the backstory for Lycians be that they were rare before the resurgence, and not a new phenomenon. Rather, in my home campaigns, similar beings were fairly common in some places and circumstances, embodying the new mythologies of the modern world. Chimera associated with Sports Team Mascots, the Lottery, the Zodiac, Industry and a wide assortment of Urban Legends were downright common in the Near Dreaming.<br /> <br /> So I find myself pondering PC and NPC concepts for Lycians. How to best portray these beings in a game, both as play character &quot;templates&quot; and suggestions and for the use of storytelling.<br /> <br /> I am curious about what you all think of the Lycians and what you might do with these creatures in your games? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T11:53:42-07:00","id":1310332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1310325-lycian-characters-c20-player-guide#post1310325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, I love the concept of Chimera player characters. I generally allow such creatures for players that cannot make regular gaming sessions, and as &quot;stock&quot; characters for new players. And the Lycians allow such characters suitable for main characters.<br /> <br /> For my own use as a Storyteller, I would have the backstory for Lycians be that they were rare before the resurgence, and not a new phenomenon. Rather, in my home campaigns, similar beings were fairly common in some places and circumstances, embodying the new mythologies of the modern world. Chimera associated with Sports Team Mascots, the Lottery, the Zodiac, Industry and a wide assortment of Urban Legends were downright common in the Near Dreaming.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was teh canon or did I misread?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T11:57:21-07:00","id":1310333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1310325-lycian-characters-c20-player-guide?p=1310332#post1310332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that was teh canon or did I misread?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Page 104 states: &quot;Lycian chimera, however, are a recent phenomenon.&quot; And that the Inanimae are working hard to understand them. <br /> <br /> All of which is fine for the metaplot. But for my purposes I would have them as present in other times. Perhaps being the many nature and city spirits of the Nunnehi, Kwannon-Jin (rather than using Umbrood) and others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 05-06-2019, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T04:29:59-07:00","id":1310509,"title":"","content":"Just got the book and read over these guys... it occurs to me that they would make a great Toy Story campaign....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1407,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","user":"EndlessKng","date":". 05-07-2019, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T06:44:00-07:00","id":1310525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1310325-lycian-characters-c20-player-guide?p=1310509#post1310509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just got the book and read over these guys... it occurs to me that they would make a great Toy Story campaign....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fun fact: a couple of things were cut for space. One of them was a sidebar of inspirational resources for Lycian chronicles in which the Toy Story movies were mentioned by name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T07:13:50-07:00","id":1310528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1310325-lycian-characters-c20-player-guide?p=1310525#post1310525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact: a couple of things were cut for space. One of them was a sidebar of inspirational resources for Lycian chronicles in which the Toy Story movies were mentioned by name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might we see some of these cut bits? I for one will be allowing Lycian characters in my campaigns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T09:17:53-07:00","id":1310551,"title":"","content":"I'll see what I can do. If I'm able to, I'll probably post it as a free download on Storyteller's Vault so it'll always be easily accessible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T09:54:03-07:00","id":1310558,"title":"","content":"While we have a thread for it I did have a question to clarify.<br /> <br /> There seems to be a disconnect between origin and guise and the object the Lycian arises from. For instance, the example of the Mustang, representing freedom of the road, is listed as having a human form (on the human/animal/mythic axis) and represents a concept but is embodied in an object. Does the Lycian appear humanoid in the dreaming or am I misunderstanding the connection? It seemed like they are supposed to manifest in the form of whatever they are, but that seemed to imply an anthropomorphic avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T10:20:54-07:00","id":1310566,"title":"","content":"Their Shape is like a changeling's fae mein, while their Guise is sort of like a mortal seeming. They're all mundane things that have awakened and gained a chimerical overlay in the process. How that manifests is going to vary a lot from Lycian to Lycian, even between ones with the same Guise and Shape. A Lycian whose Guise is a car and Shape is humanoid might manifest as a person who rides along with the driver in a passenger seat or sits on the hood or trunk to talk to people outside the car or even the car's diver when the Lycian is moving about on their own. On the other hand, a Lycian whose Guise is a sea shell and Shape is humanoid might appear chimercially as a person wearing the sea shell as a necklace or a helmet or a ring or might just have some qualities that evoke a feeling of a sea shell while the mundane sea shell itself is completely subsumed within their chimerical form.<br /> <br /> It's really limited only by the imagination of the player or Storyteller. The one caveat is that Guise and Shape are inseparable unless the Lycian possesses the Two Places at Once rede.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 05-07-2019, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T10:42:46-07:00","id":1310573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1310325-lycian-characters-c20-player-guide?p=1310566#post1310566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On the other hand, a Lycian whose Guise is a sea shell and Shape is humanoid might appear chimercially as a person wearing the sea shell as a necklace or a helmet or a ring or might just have some qualities that evoke a feeling of a sea shell while the mundane sea shell itself is completely subsumed within their chimerical form.<br /> <br /> It's really limited only by the imagination of the player or Storyteller. The one caveat is that Guise and Shape are inseparable unless the Lycian possesses the Two Places at Once rede.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Sea Shell example above, the humanoid form would be entirely chimerical/ephemera? It would need Wyrd to have a body in the Autumn world? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T10:55:32-07:00","id":1310577,"title":"","content":"To the unenchanted, yeah, the sea shell is just a sea shell. If it wants to do something impossible for a sea shell to do and there's a mortal onlooker, the Lycian needs the Wyrd rede or to convince their Changeling Companion to Call the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Edit: <s>or risk gaining Banality, assuming the mortal onlooker's Banality isn't too high.</s><br /> <br /> Edit 2: Forgot we're talking about a humanoid Lycian. Their Shape protects them from Banality due to mortal witnesses because it's easier for the Mists to blur people's perceptions about what's actually going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 05-07-2019, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T15:38:30-07:00","id":1310627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1310325-lycian-characters-c20-player-guide?p=1310577#post1310577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the unenchanted, yeah, the sea shell is just a sea shell. If it wants to do something impossible for a sea shell to do and there's a mortal onlooker, the Lycian needs the Wyrd rede or to convince their Changeling Companion to Call the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Edit: <s>or risk gaining Banality, assuming the mortal onlooker's Banality isn't too high.</s><br /> <br /> Edit 2: Forgot we're talking about a humanoid Lycian. Their Shape protects them from Banality due to mortal witnesses because it's easier for the Mists to blur people's perceptions about what's actually going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Got it now. Between your two posts you made it super clear and I appreciate it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T16:05:43-07:00","id":1311892,"title":"","content":"Ok I have a couple of questions:<br /> <br /> What is the Thematic Difference between a Mannikin and a Lycian? What makes some concept fall on one side or the other?<br /> <br /> Ok Second, are most Lycians like.. Buzz or Woody? Should they be going around thinking they are a spaceman/magical girl etc or should they IN General know what they are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T11:52:09-07:00","id":1312134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1310325-lycian-characters-c20-player-guide?p=1311892#post1311892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok I have a couple of questions:<br /> <br /> What is the Thematic Difference between a Mannikin and a Lycian? What makes some concept fall on one side or the other?</div> </div> </div> </div>Inanimae are, on the whole, classic elementals. Lycians are elementals of the Anthropocene.<br /> <br /> Inanimae and Lycians have a certain amount of overlap \u2014 they're both fundamentally stories about living objects. The Inanimae themselves see enough similarities to believe the Lycians are new dream destined to usurp their place in the Dreaming someday. From an in-game perspective, the biggest difference between them is that the Inanimae are immortal faerie souls inhabiting an object to protect themselves against Banality while Lycians are simply an inanimate object that's accumulated enough Glamour to awaken as a chimera. A Lycian's existence is much more temporary than an Inanimae's.<br /> <br /> Out of game, it really depends on the kinds of stories you want to tell. Inanimae are, like other changelings, immortals that have lived many lifetimes and will probably continue living even after their current body is destroyed. They just need to find a new Anchor. Lycians have only one life to live and are inseparable from their Guises. A teddy bear Mannikin has probably lived longer than the child she currently plays with and will likely continue living long after the child passes away. A teddy bear Lycian has only ever known the child who gave her life and will probably die when the child outgrows her.<br /> <br /> [Edit to add: Inanimae are also more in control of their own destiny. Like other changelings, they're the masters of dreams. They have an Antithesis, but as long as they don't cross it, they can do whatever they want. Lycians are chimera, so they're ruled by the dream that birthed them. They have a Thesis which governs what they can and can't do.]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok Second, are most Lycians like.. Buzz or Woody? Should they be going around thinking they are a spaceman/magical girl etc or should they IN General know what they are? </div> </div> </div>I'd say the proportion of Lycians who know they're a chimera vs believe they're actually a spaceman or whatever is about the same as it for any other chimera. In other words, do what works best for your game and the kinds of stories you're telling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 05-14-2019, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T14:12:04-07:00","id":1312152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1310325-lycian-characters-c20-player-guide?p=1312134#post1312134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Inanimae are, on the whole, classic elementals. Lycians are elementals of the Anthropocene.<br /> <br /> Inanimae and Lycians have a certain amount of overlap \u2014 they're both fundamentally stories about living objects. The Inanimae themselves see enough similarities to believe the Lycians are new dream destined to usurp their place in the Dreaming someday. From an in-game perspective, the biggest difference between them is that the Inanimae are immortal faerie souls inhabiting an object to protect themselves against Banality while Lycians are simply an inanimate object that's accumulated enough Glamour to awaken as a chimera. A Lycian's existence is much more temporary than an Inanimae's.<br /> <br /> Out of game, it really depends on the kinds of stories you want to tell. Inanimae are, like other changelings, immortals that have lived many lifetimes and will probably continue living even after their current body is destroyed. They just need to find a new Anchor. Lycians have only one life to live and are inseparable from their Guises. A teddy bear Mannikin has probably lived longer than the child she currently plays with and will likely continue living long after the child passes away. A teddy bear Lycian has only ever known the child who gave her life and will probably die when the child outgrows her.<br /> <br /> [Edit to add: Inanimae are also more in control of their own destiny. Like other changelings, they're the masters of dreams. They have an Antithesis, but as long as they don't cross it, they can do whatever they want. Lycians are chimera, so they're ruled by the dream that birthed them. They have a Thesis which governs what they can and can't do.]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That helps some but I'm honestly I think that makes it harder for me grok the Empire of Flickers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd say the proportion of Lycians who know they're a chimera vs believe they're actually a spaceman or whatever is about the same as it for any other chimera. In other words, do what works best for your game and the kinds of stories you're telling. </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly not sure what's best. I Can see advantages to both<br /> <br /> <br /> Thirdish question: Could a Lycian be a Chimerical companion(the background?) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T08:03:45-07:00","id":1312570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1310325-lycian-characters-c20-player-guide?p=1312152#post1312152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That helps some but I'm honestly I think that makes it harder for me grok the Empire of Flickers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might help to think of the Empire of Flickers as the Inanimae faction that is actively trying to evolve the Inanimae for the modern Dreaming. They're probably the ones most actively trying to synthesize the Inanimae dream and the Lycian dream so that when destiny eventually strikes, the Inanimae can thrive instead of being displaced.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thirdish question: Could a Lycian be a Chimerical companion(the background?) </div> </div> </div>They can take the Changeling Companion background, which implies that they're a changeling's Chimerical Companion. I'm pretty sure the Views from Without section also talks a bit about Kithain, Inanimae, and Thallain having Lycian Chimerical Companions. So yeah, I don't see why not. If I were STing and one of my players wanted to take a Lycian Chimerical Companion, I'd probably just use the standard Chimerical Companion rules for simplicity's sake with the NPC's Lycian nature being story based instead of rules based. As always though, whatever works best for your play style and your gaming group is the best way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T09:15:46-07:00","id":1312582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1310325-lycian-characters-c20-player-guide?p=1312570#post1312570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It might help to think of the Empire of Flickers as the Inanimae faction that is actively trying to evolve the Inanimae for the modern Dreaming. They're probably the ones most actively trying to synthesize the Inanimae dream and the Lycian dream so that when destiny eventually strikes, the Inanimae can thrive instead of being displaced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so we're on the same page, that's the Inanimae of artificial light, yeah? 'Cause the Empire of Flickers keeps getting associated with mannikins in C20, who're the Empire of Dolls.<br /> <br /> Any chance of the Empire of artificial light ever getting covered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T10:12:51-07:00","id":1312592,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but by the nature of the phyla, the Empire of Flickers is going to be limited to certain ones. Mannikins and solimonds are probably the vast majority, if not the exclusive members of, the empire with the fewest Inanimae.<br /> <br /> As for if there will ever be more word count devoted to Flickers, only time will tell. I have no inside information, but my guess is that Player's Guide sales numbers will determine if we get any more source books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T10:39:50-07:00","id":1312599,"title":"","content":"Right, I get it - Flickers generally takes its members from other phyla, rather than having a signature phyla of its own. Gotcha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T06:47:57-07:00","id":1312746,"title":"","content":"Mannikins are an evolutionary step, defined by subjective perception of the human shape rather than material. The Empire of Flickers are the inanimae eqivalent of transhumanists as chimerical postmodernists","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T09:51:19-07:00","id":1312780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>El Barto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1310325-lycian-characters-c20-player-guide?p=1312746#post1312746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mannikins are an evolutionary step, defined by subjective perception of the human shape rather than material. The Empire of Flickers are the inanimae eqivalent of transhumanists as chimerical postmodernists</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That does put the situation of Crofted Inanimae into question... if I make a Wooden Puppet it could be an anchor for mannikin.. but also a Kubara","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T10:11:21-07:00","id":1312787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1310325-lycian-characters-c20-player-guide?p=1312780#post1312780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That does put the situation of Crofted Inanimae into question... if I make a Wooden Puppet it could be an anchor for mannikin.. but also a Kubara</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! Likewise, if the Anchor is one of those wooden console TVs from the 70's and 80's, do you have a mannikin, solimond, or kubara? Which Empire does the Inanimae belong to? I'd say the answer ultimately comes down to what sort of character concept the players has in mind.<br /> <br /> I'd also say we're straying pretty far from the actual topic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T19:50:23-07:00","id":1312868,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=PookaKnight;n1312570]<br /> <br /> It might help to think of the Empire of Flickers as the Inanimae faction that is actively trying to evolve the Inanimae for the modern Dreaming. They're probably the ones most actively trying to synthesize the Inanimae dream and the Lycian dream so that when destiny eventually strikes, the Inanimae can thrive instead of being displaced.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can take the Changeling Companion background, which implies that they're a changeling's Chimerical Companion. I'm pretty sure the Views from Without section also talks a bit about Kithain, Inanimae, and Thallain having Lycian Chimerical Companions. So yeah, I don't see why not. If I were STing and one of my players wanted to take a Lycian Chimerical Companion, I'd probably just use the standard Chimerical Companion rules for simplicity's sake with the NPC's Lycian nature being story based instead of rules based. As always though, whatever works best for your play style and your gaming group is the best way to go. </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm unhappy with Infusion as is currently written but I had a bit of an epiphany. A way to make Gigul/Its Alive more broadly functional than just Fae 5.. to allow the Creation of Lycans.. or is that Too powerful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-19T16:42:08-07:00","id":1313216,"title":"","content":"What Backgrounds are really okay for a Lycian to pick up? A floater in my group is thinking of playing one when he's able to attend sessions. Would love to hear everyone's opinions, the bit we get in the book leaves me with a few questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T05:16:15-08:00","id":1352790,"title":"","content":"Reviving this old thread, since the &quot;overlay&quot; answers from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar648_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"648\" data-vbnamecard=\"648\">PookaKnight</a> helped clear up a lot of confusion about the Shape vs Guise dilemma.<br /> <br /> So, if Roma's Guise is &quot;the GPS coordinates of Rome,&quot; would it be that she can appear anywhere within Rome, or to teleport between any phone or computer that had a Google Maps open with Rome (&quot;All Roads lead to Rome. Even on the Internet Superhighway&quot;)? Or is this itself a matter of ST interpretation?<br /> <br /> Is there a particular &quot;limit&quot; to how large a Guise itself can be? For example, if one wanted to make Old Ironsides as an Oppidian that was anchored to the USS Constitution, would there be any mechanical disadvantage there, beyond the Constitution being anchored/it presumably requiring the Two Places At Once Rede?<br /> <br /> Can a Lycian be &quot;forced&quot; out of its anchor, or used as a material to create a Treasure, and if so, could it thus have Glamour Pact? <br /> <br /> The Bucolic example of the albino deer confuses me. Is the deer itself the Guise? I thought only inanimate items could be Guise proper?<br /> <br /> Say there is an oddball case: The stirrups from the Lone Ranger set are now the Guise for a Maeutic Animal (a horse) representing &quot;The Good Cowboy.&quot; Say a Kithain dons the stirrups, mounting the horse, and goes &quot;Hi Ho, Silver, Away!&quot; Riding off to save the day, both parties forget to Wyrd the Lycian, and they come across some confused townfolk...How does the Banality trigger resolution resolve then?<br /> <br /> How do you track &quot;lethal damage&quot; for a Guise that exists as an abstract concept by the way?<br /> <br /> Also, I assume a Lycian doesn't get the same rate of accelerated Glamour regen as a normal Chimera, while in the Dreaming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","user":"MagicJuggler","date":". 12-05-2019, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}